{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Cooking Accident", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Quick Thinking", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 10, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe  events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Suggestions and Offers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use modals like  <span class=\"italic\">could</span> and <span class=\"italic\">can</span> to make offers or to give suggestions. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Could</span> with <span class=\"italic\">you/we</span> is frequently used to make suggestions or offers. <span class=\"italic\">Could</span> shows that the suggestion or offer is an option.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You could go watch a movie.</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">We could go for a walk.</span></li></ul><br/> <span class=\"italic\">Should</span> with <span class=\"italic\">you</span> is used to make strong suggestions, like advice.<br/> <ul><li><span class=\"italic\">You should find out what you missed while you were sick.</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You should go home early tonight.</li> <li><span class=\"italic\">You should study accounting.</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Sentence</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Meaning</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You could make up little recipe booklets for the restaurant.<br/><br/>   I can pass them along.<br/><br/>   You should give me a couple to take to the office.<br/><br/>  You should hire me to do some PR. <br/><br/>  By the way, you should cut away from yourself.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's a good option.<br/><br/>    It's an option.<br/><br/>  It's a strong suggestion.<br/><br/>   It's a strong suggestion.<br/><br/>   It's a strong suggestion.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modal Verbs in the Passive Voice", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modal verbs to add meaning to other verbs. They come before the dictionary form (Infinitive without \u2018to') of the main verb.  Modal verbs can add meaning connected with certainty or obligation.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use modal verbs in the passive voice. <br/> You use the passive voice when you want to focus on the receiver of the action, rather than the \u2018doer' of the action. <br/><br/>  Here is the structure of a passive sentence:<br/><br/>  Subject + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">The booklets <span class=\"strong\">are sent</span> as a thank you to Ms. Ryan.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can add a modal verb before the <span class=\"italic\">to be</span>:<br/><br/>  Subject + modal + to be + past participle<br/><br/>  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">The booklets <span class=\"strong\">could be sent</span> as a thank you to Ms. Ryan.</span><br/><br/>  Here the sentence now has an additional meaning of possibility, thanks to the modal <span class=\"strong\">could</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "They could be put out to sell at our next Spicy Rice Night! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You can't be trusted with knives!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "That was brilliant of you explaining  how everything could be fixed!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Accidents can be prevented when you pay attention to what you're doing.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bleed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lose blood", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You're bleeding. You should get that wound bandaged.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you cook at home.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to make up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to invent; to create", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should make up little recipe booklets for the restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to put out ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to offer", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They could be put out to sell at our next Spicy Rice Night!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "booklet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a small and thin book", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our recipes come in little booklets.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "PR", "type": "name"}, {"content": "Public Relations; the business of giving the public information about a particular organization or person in order to create a good impression", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You should hire me to do some PR.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to trust", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have confidence in a person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't be trusted sometimes!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "profitable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "beneficial and productive", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It helped make the evening even more profitable!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "standing reservation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an arrangement or plan occurring at a regular time", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I even got a standing reservation from one of her crew.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crew", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of people working together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: One of her crew made a reservation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le10ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm accidents that can can happen when cooking in the kitchen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now make notes stating how these things can be avoided.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Find or draw some pictures to help illustrate your ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now, put together your pamphlet on preventing accidents in the kitchen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Take it to class and present it to other students.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm accidents that can can happen when cooking in the kitchen.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make notes on how these can be avoided.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I find or draw picture to illustrate the ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make up my pamphlet.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my pamphlet with others.", "type